change:
  id: CHG-028
  title: Generation CLI failure semantics
  status: proposed
  intent: Make generation failure exits, abort journalling, runtime validation errors and ranking alignment clear and consistent for CLI users and automation.
  audience_level: developer
  relates_to:
    - RISK-009
    - PAT-004
    - RISK-003

deltas:
  - op: ADDED
    capability: mutation-fitness-loop
    requirement: A multi-candidate generation that completes with no evidence exits 1 after printing one line that says no candidate produced evidence and names the first failure; a generation with evidence still exits 0, and a single-candidate run is unchanged.
    scenarios:
      - id: S1
        when: every candidate in a generation fails to produce evidence, such as a rerun using existing candidate worktrees
        then: the command exits 1, reports the first failure, and prints the journal path
      - id: S2
        when: a generation aborts after one or more candidates were evaluated, such as a proposer repeating a mutation id
        then: the journal appends an aborted-generation entry with the evaluated count and reason before the failure propagates
      - id: S3
        when: an option value is rejected during command execution, or a run fails for any other reason
        then: a rejected option value is thrown as a picocli ParameterException and renders exactly as a parse error does - its message, then usage, exit 2; any other failure prints one "error:" line to stderr and exits 1, with no usage and no stack trace
        and:
          - the split is by exception type at the point of throw, not by root cause. An earlier draft classified any IllegalArgumentException root cause as a usage error, which would have shown usage for a domain validation failure deep inside a run, as though the user had mistyped a flag
          - a message relayed from Git ends in a newline; the handler strips it, which the runtime-failure test found by asserting one line rather than a prefix
          - the error line keeps every distinct message in the cause chain, outermost first, so "failed to read ablation corpus: /missing.tsv" says what failed as well as why. The first version printed only the root cause, which reduced that to the bare path
          - an unknown --operator is a bad option value and renders as one, closing the same two-presentations split RISK-009 named for --candidates
      - id: S4
        when: ranked candidates have ids longer than forty characters and different lengths
        then: score and decision columns align to the longest id in that generation

acceptance:
  - scenario: S1
    test_id: cli/EvolveGenerationAcceptanceTest.aGenerationWhereNoCandidateProducesEvidenceExitsOneAndNamesTheFirstFailure
    layer: acceptance
  - scenario: S2
    test_id: adapters/EvolveRunnerTest.aGenerationThatAbortsRecordsItsEvaluatedCountAndReasonBeforePropagating
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S3
    test_id: cli/EvolveCommandAcceptanceTest.rendersRuntimeOptionValidationLikeAParseError
    layer: acceptance
  - scenario: S3
    test_id: cli/EvolveCommandAcceptanceTest.rendersARuntimeFailureAsOneErrorLineWithoutUsageOrStackTrace
    layer: acceptance
  - scenario: S3
    test_id: cli/MutationLoopCliTest.aMissingAblationCorpusSaysWhatFailedNotOnlyThePath
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S3
    test_id: cli/MutationLoopCliTest.anUnknownOperatorIsABadOptionValueAndRendersAsOne
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S2
    test_id: deterministic/GenerationEvaluationLoopTest.aFailingAbortReporterDoesNotReplaceTheAbortCause
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S4
    test_id: cli/ConsoleReporterTest.reportsTheGenerationOrderWinnerEvidenceCountAndSpread
    layer: unit

tasks:
  - id: T1
    slice: Report and fail a completed no-evidence generation while preserving the single-candidate path
    status: completed
  - id: T2
    slice: Append a journal abort record before a generation failure propagates
    status: completed
  - id: T3
    slice: Install the shared top-level picocli execution-exception policy
    status: completed
  - id: T4
    slice: Size ranking columns from the current generation and widen the fixture
    status: completed

non_goals:
  - an aborted-generation ledger row
  - changing one-candidate run semantics
  - a new verbose stack-trace option or environment variable

risks:
  - The abort journal is a human-readable audit trail rather than a ledger entry. The journal append precedes propagation, while a durable structured abort ledger requires a separately designed schema and replay policy.
  - The execution handler deliberately centralises presentation only. It does not convert runtime failures into successful commands or hide test-level exceptions from code that invokes command handlers directly.
